## Requirements

- **Python 3.8+**
- No external dependencies (uses only `math` from standard library)

## Development

```bash
# Clone and install in development mode
git clone https://github.com/marc1fino/marksgeometrys.git
cd marksgeometrys
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # or .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1 on Windows
pip install -e .

# Run tests
python -c "
from marksgeometrys import Square, Cube, Octohedron, Sphere
assert Square(side=5).area() == 25
assert Cube(side=3).volume() == 27
assert Octohedron(side=3).volume() is not None  # Bug fixed
assert Sphere(radius=1).area_formatted().endswith('cm²')
print('All tests passed!')
"
```

## Version History

- **0.1.1** — Current release
  - Numeric returns for `area()` / `volume()`
  - Added `unit` parameter to all classes
  - Added `area_formatted()` / `volume_formatted()` methods
  - Fixed Octohedron returning `None` for non-zero sides
  - Proper squared/cubed unit notation (cm², cm³, mm², m³, etc.)

## Roadmap

- Add perimeter/circumference methods for 2D shapes
- Add moment of inertia calculations for 3D solids
- Support for composite figures
- Spherical coordinates and vector operations
- Type hints and full mypy compatibility
- Comprehensive test suite with pytest

